{"title":"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(non-rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (non-rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular box <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in a sphere of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. The surface area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is 384, and the sum of the lengths of its <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> edges is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd3907e89ce5b06f13d78589b5d92624a8b41a7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$112$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a193fdc02ba5e2119ed54b22de44c79050f0fb25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 8\\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 10\\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 12\\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 14\\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"381\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Box P has dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. \nIts surface area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a76b6404f3224d41af7694e99206d9c5b4b67f1f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2lw+2lh+2wh=384,\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"16\" /> \nand the sum of all its edges is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/86391c1d6be352d4b06253140f65e260ee99b750.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[l + w + h = \\dfrac{4l+4w+4h}{4} = \\dfrac{112}{4} = 28.\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The diameter of the sphere is the space diagonal of the prism, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/31384be5c4dd31ee79fefadd8f754b0e543415a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{l^2 + w^2 +h^2}.\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />\nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/732402136a72c8702e21e92822de90d0ec99a4bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}(l + w + h)^2 - (2lw + 2lh + 2wh) &amp;= l^2 + w^2 + h^2 \\\\ &amp;= 784 - 384 \\\\ &amp;= 400,\\end{align*}\" width=\"381\" height=\"69\" /> so the diameter is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8ab71d91a8a41cd30d5290648d0c972a78086d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{l^2 + w^2 +h^2} = \\sqrt{400} = 20.\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"18\" /> The radius is half of the diameter, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b53a7d5494de9713624c690fe8aeb4422c24c07.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=\\frac{20}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 10}.\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28non-rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(non-rigorous)\">Solution 2 (non-rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (non-rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in the previous solution, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/7573e1ffb29899fde3036b4740490455539640cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2lw+2lh+2wh=384$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"182\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdc6741dcd1c99f0cc64e882d627ee2f4d8f9a73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l + w + h = \\dfrac{4l+4w+4h}{4} = \\dfrac{112}{4} = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"301\" height=\"38\" />, and the diameter of the sphere is the space diagonal of the prism, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29e8e6e3d99747113eb02f253c58ad85c84a5e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{l^2 + w^2 + h^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now, since this is competition math, we only need to find the space diagonal of any one box that fits the requirements, so assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/7/af7e5b7d062655d4be01f4d56b203954a93cf7eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. (This essentially means that we have an infinitesimally thin box.) We now have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b1eb3e739a9dff4e57ce5e4f6f8181e99a8b7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2lw = 384$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4fde207552da64bf77596e6c2c6fce77a6794b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l + w = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, and we are solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb20539f40591605344b5b0baf7769ec68f510be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{l^2 + w^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa3197b4a4bb9adcc63c6b5ca5fc56c1652d8624.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}(l + w)^2 - 2lw &amp;= l^2 + 2lw + w^2 - 2lw \\\\ &amp;= l^2 + w^2,\\end{align*}\" width=\"293\" height=\"46\" /> this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf3fd795d2a9dc3f688e52f7a4b66dcd9e5fba2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[l^2 + w^2 = 28^2 - 384 = 400,\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"18\" /> so the space diagonal is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77e20ed59fa013138bee79301b0dd31534880a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{400} = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />. Since the diameter of the sphere is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a368110dca16f12cbb152ecfdb72ec11029ee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />. ~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Emerald_block\" title=\"User:Emerald block\">emerald_block</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A\">2005 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2005 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017204743\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.044 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.070 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 238/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5274/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   19.506      1 -total\n 57.71%   11.256      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 39.69%    7.742      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5198:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017204743 and revision id 253035. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}